From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the scene data's reflection colour a vec4

Since #112178 (4.8-dev7), SceneData holds the reflection colour as a
vec3 followed by a uint. On Metal, SPIRV-Cross turns that vec3 into a
packed_float3, and multiview draws (XR's stereo, where the shader picks
each eye's matrices from the same block by view index) became 10 to 15
times slower: 21.6 ms of GPU time a frame against 1.65 ms for the same
two eyes drawn as single views, at 1664 by 1792 per eye on an M4 Max.

Declaring it as a vec4 keeps the same 16 bytes, so the C++ side
(float[3] and a pad) is unchanged, and Metal no longer packs it.

Test: an XR viewport with two views (an XRInterfaceExtension is
enough) on Metal; its GPU time matches two single views (1.62 ms).

Upstream: to propose; regression from godotengine/godot#112178.
---
 .../rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_data_inc.glsl        | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_data_inc.glsl b/godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_data_inc.glsl
index 7437b48e..55b72d3d 100644
--- a/godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_data_inc.glsl
+++ b/godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_data_inc.glsl
@@ -61,8 +61,9 @@ struct SceneData {
 
 	vec4 ambient_light_color_energy;
 
-	vec3 reflection_color;
-	uint pad;
+	// A vec4 (rgb used), not a vec3 and a uint: Metal's shaders would hold a vec3 here as a
+	// packed float3, which makes multiview passes many times slower.
+	vec4 reflection_color;
 
 	float ambient_color_sky_mix;
 	float fog_density;
